{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19","id":1308892,"title":"Monday Meeting 29/4/19","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-29T22:46:41-07:00","id":1308892,"title":"Monday Meeting 29/4/19","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/its-in-the-cards-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">Exigents is now in first drafts.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T01:27:23-07:00","id":1308899,"title":"","content":"\u30fe(\uff65\u03c9\uff65*)\uff89\u2740\u30c5\u2764\u266b<br /> <br /> \u00b0\\(^\u25bf^)/\u00b0<br /> <br /> \u2517(\uff3e0\uff3e)\u2513","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T09:15:55-07:00","id":1308938,"title":"","content":"Interesting.<br /> <br /> I wonder when we'll see any previews. Unlike DBs and Lunars, I have no real preconceptions, particular things I want to see, etc. So I'm not really excited by Exigents per-se, but something new and inspiring could make a big difference.<br /> Especially the different kinds of Exigents (and non-Exigents) shown in the book, which are all very new.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T12:13:27-07:00","id":1308985,"title":"","content":"if we get previews my guess is that it would probably be about the four example Exigents they have in the book, like Janest","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T13:00:44-07:00","id":1308995,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... with the previous two splats, they did three previews I think? A couple of mechanics previews, and a fluff preview? Something like that?<br /> <br /> The thing of course, is that it was three previews about Lunars, or three previews about Dragonblood.<br /> Exigents is a bit different.<br /> Will they do, say, a preview of one of the four example Exigent types? A preview of something general about Exigents, for example the charm-creation rules or fluff about the Exigence itself? Will they do any previews for the three other kinds of Exalts in the appendix or not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T14:14:28-07:00","id":1309011,"title":"","content":"Since they just posted it, they probably only just hired the writers. I\u2019d expect it to be a month or two before we saw anything at all.<br /> <br /> I also expect Exigents to be much harder to write than any other splat book ever, so I\u2019m trying very hard not to have any timeline expectations for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T00:47:55-07:00","id":1309131,"title":"","content":"Oh, I certainly don't expect previews for months. Probably August or something.<br /> <br /> I think Exigents is very difficult to write, but I don't know if it'll be longer. It may have a lot less charms, since it's about making your own charmset.<br /> It also may have less fluff, as it has no organisation that needs a chapter like the Silver Pact, Realm, etc.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's going to contain 7 sets of character gen rules+traits+charmsets, so there may be just as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T08:19:03-07:00","id":1309178,"title":"","content":"The biggest thing I'm curious about is how the hell they're going to do stretch goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T08:28:52-07:00","id":1309182,"title":"","content":"More example Exigents would be the obvious one. They could also do more charms or something for the non-canonical Exalt types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T08:56:21-07:00","id":1309192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1309131#post1309131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I certainly don't expect previews for months. Probably August or something.<br /> <br /> I think Exigents is very difficult to write, but I don't know if it'll be longer. It may have a lot less charms, since it's about making your own charmset.<br /> It also may have less fluff, as it has no organisation that needs a chapter like the Silver Pact, Realm, etc.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's going to contain 7 sets of character gen rules+traits+charmsets, so there may be just as much.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It has four sample sets of Exigent Charms, a couple of which have been confirmed, so it does have a ton of Charms. To put it into perspective, book's so big that they cannot put any Martial Arts, Sorcery or Artifacts in it, though with its rules you can make your own much easier I'd hope. Though unfortunately we're not getting Charms for the optional Exalts as far as we've heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","user":"Alistair","date":". 05-01-2019, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T09:16:44-07:00","id":1309195,"title":"","content":"Well they said there would be notes on what their charms should be like. If the info on building charms is good, then it shouldn\u2019t be too difficult to make them playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T09:19:08-07:00","id":1309196,"title":"","content":"Oh really? I didn't realise that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T09:19:09-07:00","id":1309197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1309195#post1309195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they said there would be notes on what their charms should be like. If the info on building charms is good, then it shouldn\u2019t be too difficult to make them playable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed! It's just more of a &quot;Build it yourself&quot; deal. But four Charmsets is pretty damn good as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T09:25:38-07:00","id":1309202,"title":"","content":"If I was going to do stretch goals for Exigents, one thing I would plan on doing was making sure that the appendix with the extra exalts went out in the middle of the KS. That would give a bit of time for everyone to absorb the info. Then, if we hit enough goals, maybe we have a stretch goal that lets us vote for one of them to be expanded in the companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T09:39:50-07:00","id":1309211,"title":"","content":"Have they stated they intend to do a Kickstarter for Exigents? Or is that just presumed based on general &quot;splat books get Kickstarted&quot; mindset? I asked in the Devs thread but only because it caught my attention here that we're presuming there will be one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T09:41:51-07:00","id":1309212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1309211#post1309211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have they stated they intend to do a Kickstarter for Exigents? Or is that just presumed based on general &quot;splat books get Kickstarted&quot; mindset? I asked in the Devs thread but only because it caught my attention here that we're presuming there will be one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All books except maybe Liminals and Getimians have been said to be getting a Kickstarter as far as I know. They've also talked about stretch goals for it and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T09:42:28-07:00","id":1309213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1309202#post1309202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was going to do stretch goals for Exigents, one thing I would plan on doing was making sure that the appendix with the extra exalts went out in the middle of the KS. That would give a bit of time for everyone to absorb the info. Then, if we hit enough goals, maybe we have a stretch goal that lets us vote for one of them to be expanded in the companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T15:08:58-07:00","id":1310113,"title":"","content":"What fortuitous timing; if anything could bring me back, it's Exigents. That's exciting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","name":"Heart Attacks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25282_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T00:20:42-07:00","id":1310231,"title":"","content":"It will be pretty nice to get this book when it finally comes. For stretch goals on it the possibilities are endless really. Additional Charm sets, additional exigent examples, additional general type charms, new sorceries, spells, literally anything. It is a book that has a ton of ground to cover but everything I have seen from this team so fr I believe they will pull it off brilliantly. With this much of an advanced warning I will have plenty of time to save up.<br /> <br /> For a side question, what are you all wishing they would have in the stretch goals or add ons that would excite you? A couple things I hope to see a listed below.<br /> <br /> Cloth Map (They are just to awesome love them)<br /> Paper money replicas. (Possibly even house examples?)<br /> 3D printing blueprints or a partner that will print possibly some miniatures for Exalted<br /> Ink stamp of some house or other powers forces<br /> some coin replicas of Dinars<br /> <br /> Love to hear everyone else's thoughts on this as well. I personally love having a physical item or prop to use as a player and ST.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T15:24:03-07:00","id":1310392,"title":"","content":"What would the cloth map of though? The only thing that pops up is Great Forks but I think that's to small. That and Yu Shan though I'd think they would save that for Sidereals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T00:28:19-07:00","id":1310490,"title":"","content":"The best stretch goal for the fan would be &quot;We will write a charmset for your Exigent&quot;, but that will never happen \ud83d\ude22","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T02:39:56-07:00","id":1310502,"title":"","content":"Need real precise charms creation rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13553-kenshinzen","name":"Kenshinzen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13553_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T04:14:40-07:00","id":1310508,"title":"","content":"I'd love more charmsets of Exigents that were in the Core Book as a stretch goal, especially the Chosen of Seals, Masks, or Dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1310490#post1310490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best stretch goal for the fan would be &quot;We will write a charmset for your Exigent&quot;, but that will never happen \ud83d\ude22</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see them making a &quot;Miracles of the Solar Exalted&quot; type addon with less open slots but where each contributor gets a general description of their exigent + a few charms to get started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T06:08:06-07:00","id":1310520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1310490#post1310490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best stretch goal for the fan would be &amp;quot;We will write a charmset for your Exigent&amp;quot;, but that will never happen \ud83d\ude22</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... It has potential actually, if it doesn't have to be too exact, and they're going to put in some more anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T09:39:48-07:00","id":1310555,"title":"","content":"Reward Tier possibility: we will stat up your Exigent as a starting character with the necessary out of the gate Charms for the Companion (not a complete set, you\u2019ll have to do the growth yourself, but enough for them to be fully playable from go)<br /> <br /> That could perhaps be priced around the same as a custom Artifact.<br /> <br /> <br /> Stretch Goals will be harder. What we want are additional full Exigent Charmsets beyond the 4 in the book, but making those stretch goals will have to be very high priced and spaced out. I certainly would love to see the Chosen of Dice, Seals, etc show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-07-2019, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T09:49:12-07:00","id":1310556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1310555#post1310555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reward Tier possibility: we will stay up your Exigent as a starting character with the necessary out of the gate Charms for the Companion (not a complete set, you\u2019ll have to do the growth yourself, but enough for them to be fully playable from go)</div> </div> </div> </div>That works.<br /> <br /> I was thinking essentially, that if they're going to put in extra charm sets anyway, they could sell the &quot;theme&quot; of the charmset. But then, the themes people suggest may not inspire the devs as much as their own ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T14:42:37-07:00","id":1310617,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it also seems to me that there's more potential for unintended wonkiness in such a charmset to have a greater impact with just a handful of fully realized sample Exigents slated to appear than if there's some in an artifact writeup when we have dozens of previous examples across several books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T10:24:22-07:00","id":1311011,"title":"","content":"I really want a reward tier to add new Exigents so I can fund something for Shield of a Different Day or Weaver of Dreams of Victory, but it's bound to be absurdly expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T16:41:46-07:00","id":1311304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1311011#post1311011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want a reward tier to add new Exigents so I can fund something for Shield of a Different Day or Weaver of Dreams of Victory, but it's bound to be absurdly expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>They straight out said they wouldn't do that. But options such as &quot;At this level we'll make your exigent into a chargen character with starting charms written out&quot; are not ruled out yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T12:16:08-07:00","id":1311595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1309202#post1309202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was going to do stretch goals for Exigents, one thing I would plan on doing was making sure that the appendix with the extra exalts went out in the middle of the KS. That would give a bit of time for everyone to absorb the info. Then, if we hit enough goals, maybe we have a stretch goal that lets us vote for one of them to be expanded in the companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not deciding on Kickstarter goals, and I am only writing for Exigents, but the Optional Exalted are not given shortness in the book simply out of lack of space. The reasons they were relegated to being optional were manifold: Chiefly, that even <i>after </i>reconceptualizing them from their original pitches, they simply didn't have enough narrative grist to sustain a full splat and multiple playstyles. It'd be like giving Fire Elemental God-Blooded a fatsplat.<br /> <br /> The fact that the setting is <i>lousy </i>with Exalts, and there is a book whose chief hook is, &quot;You can be any Exalt you want of virtually any conceptual god,&quot; did not help matters. Those Exalted have no history and no place in the setting. Having a lot of Exalted works for the setting of a game called <b>Exalted</b>; having them simply for the virtue of wanting more Exalted is not a good reason.<br /> <br /> And frankly, if you're going to expand one of them, you're going to have to expand all of them, lest they be seen as more canonical than the others. And they are flatly <i>not </i>canonical Exalt types, any more so than the Chosen of Nox or the Chosen of Pluto, the Maiden of Hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T11:36:16-07:00","id":1311823,"title":"","content":"I appreciate that you laid everything out like that Neall, because, from outside, it can be hard to tell if a thing is really interesting or not.<br /> <br /> From what you said, it sounds like the inherent problem with the three Optional Exalted is that there\u2019s really only one character you could create or one story you could tell for each of them, so anyone who tried to put two of them into a group might have issues making them feel sufficiently different. Is that about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T03:22:54-07:00","id":1312033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1311595#post1311595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....the Chosen of Nox or the Chosen of Pluto, the Maiden of Hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man take me back to the two plot twists of many a favorite Exalted game I have run and played in over years. They might not be Canon, but those two will always have a place in my heart, thanks for giving them a shout out Neall. ^_^<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T04:39:42-07:00","id":1312050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1311595#post1311595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not deciding on Kickstarter goals, and I am only writing for Exigents, but the Optional Exalted are not given shortness in the book simply out of lack of space. The reasons they were relegated to being optional were manifold: Chiefly, that even <i>after </i>reconceptualizing them from their original pitches, they simply didn't have enough narrative grist to sustain a full splat and multiple playstyles. It'd be like giving Fire Elemental God-Blooded a fatsplat.<br /> <br /> The fact that the setting is <i>lousy </i>with Exalts, and there is a book whose chief hook is, &amp;quot;You can be any Exalt you want of virtually any conceptual god,&amp;quot; did not help matters. Those Exalted have no history and no place in the setting. Having a lot of Exalted works for the setting of a game called <b>Exalted</b>; having them simply for the virtue of wanting more Exalted is not a good reason.<br /> <br /> And frankly, if you're going to expand one of them, you're going to have to expand all of them, lest they be seen as more canonical than the others. And they are flatly <i>not </i>canonical Exalt types, any more so than the Chosen of Nox or the Chosen of Pluto, the Maiden of Hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I appreciate the frankness on the reasoning why, I am disappointed the new exalt concepts were found inflexible\u2014I was looking forward to how these optional exalts would intertwine with the history of creation and offered new play spaces and styles, and held out hope that a popular enough reception might see them moved to full canon status. Aw well, such is life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T05:05:27-07:00","id":1312056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1312050#post1312050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I appreciate the frankness on the reasoning why, I am disappointed the new exalt concepts were found inflexible\u2014I was looking forward to how these optional exalts would intertwine with the history of creation and offered new play spaces and styles, and held out hope that a popular enough reception might see them moved to full canon status. Aw well, such is life.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much that they were &quot;found inflexible&quot; as that fully integrating a new type of Exalt into the setting is a large undertaking that requires considerable effort and takes up a significant amount of conceptual &quot;real estate&quot;\u2014compare Ex3's Lunars to those in past editions. We're already adding three new canonical Exalt types to the setting this edition; doubling that number isn't something we could do without leaving the setting totally overstuffed and giving short shrift to all of their places in it. Making them optional, and providing Storytellers who want to integrate them into the setting of their games enough detail to do so, was the best way to present them without detracting from the setting as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T05:30:45-07:00","id":1312061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1312056#post1312056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much that they were &amp;quot;found inflexible&amp;quot; as that fully integrating a new type of Exalt into the setting is a large undertaking that requires considerable effort and takes up a significant amount of conceptual &amp;quot;real estate&amp;quot;\u2014compare Ex3's Lunars to those in past editions. We're already adding three new canonical Exalt types to the setting this edition; doubling that number isn't something we could do without leaving the setting totally overstuffed and giving short shrift to all of their places in it. Making them optional, and providing Storytellers who want to integrate them into the setting of their games enough detail to do so, was the best way to present them without detracting from the setting as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, I misunderstood Nealls \u201cno history\u201d remark then. That makes more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T06:52:13-07:00","id":1312747,"title":"","content":"I should think that Exigents are a lot easier to make work than whole new Exalt groups because supporting a large character range isn't really the point.<br /> <br /> You don't need to make the Chosen of Masks capable of accomodating as many character concepts as Dragon Blooded or Chernozem, because there's only one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T05:12:52-07:00","id":1312921,"title":"","content":"I have some mixed feelings about that. <br /> <br /> On the one hand, always kind of doubted how much these splats could be fleshed out into the setting, or rather more how much the labour would be rewarded by being actually played and sold (given how mechanically intensive 3e seems in particular per splat, but how intensive almost any edition of Exalted would be that gave splats the weight of rules the audience wants). So not hugely surprised. <br /> <br /> On the other, I did enjoy the picture posed by Morke about First Age Solars in 3e surrounded by a constellation of heroes, rather than simply the classic Exalted splats, the whole lifted up by a constellation of heroes, and particularly the potential for this to defray Exalted's &quot;splatism&quot; (as MissMaddy used to call it), i.e. focus on intersplat conflicts, and to defray determinism about how splat X is necessary for outcome Y. It is something to reduce this down to Exigents as the sole firm canon expression of this (esp. if their numbers are as limited as tend to be previewed).<br /> <br /> On the whole though, it is for the best to not have the game designers producing work that they don't believe in, or don't believe is worth the labour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T11:42:09-07:00","id":1312984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1312921#post1312921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the potential for this to defray Exalted's &quot;splatism&quot; (as MissMaddy used to call it), i.e. focus on intersplat conflicts</div> </div> </div> </div>How would it have done that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">to defray determinism about how splat X is necessary for outcome Y.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though this has been helped by how the Dragon Blooded and Lunars are presented, in terms of accomplishments and ongoing projects provided to both. We have Exalted of either stripe connected to creative endeavours in a manner other than lamenting at the absence of a Solar to explain or fix it for them. Two Great Houses have secret mountain laboratories where they're working on freaky new magic, and we've got a bunch of Lunars putting together doomsday weapons (one of whom is actually not Raksi, who instead spends her time decorating her dominion with wonders and contemplating more rewarding mysteries than how to initiate a circle higher).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T12:33:20-07:00","id":1313001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1312984#post1312984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would it have done that?</div> </div> </div> </div>My vague notions that if you have a large set of Exalted who are each not significant as a splat bloc, but are collectively significant if concentrated together on a basis that is across them all as splats, then consideration of non-splat based unifying forces comes more to the fore than it otherwise would.<br /> <br /> (Those notions seem like they must be necessarily vague, because the articulation as I recall it by Morke, of the form in which the First Age was surrounded by a wealth of diverse forms of expression of Exaltation beyond what we've traditionally known, was pretty a vague and inchoate thing. But I guess I was seeking to quickly think about why that vision sounded promise for a little bit before we all immediately go off on the train of why the current vision is optimal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T13:21:30-07:00","id":1313006,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't count out Umbrals, Dream Souled and Hearteaters.<br /> <br /> Though I don't think extra words on them based on Kickstarter backing would be beneficial because it'd be responding to something that looks cool on paper or a nebulous desire for more Exalts. The question of their further development should wait until a few years down the line to see if they're still part of the conversation and holding their own once more old favourites have returned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T13:42:12-07:00","id":1313009,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1313001#post1313001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My vague notions that if you have a large set of Exalted who are each not significant as a splat bloc, but are collectively significant if concentrated together on a basis that is across them all as splats, then consideration of non-splat based unifying forces comes more to the fore than it otherwise would.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It kind of sounds more like splat-based focus along an additional axis. I think that to really get what you're talking about, the setting would need to be reworked from the ground up so that Exalted groups who have been traditionally divided are collected along lines of pure ideology.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308892-monday-meeting-29-4-19?p=1313006#post1313006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't count out Umbrals, Dream Souled and Hearteaters.<br /> <br /> Though I don't think extra words on them based on Kickstarter backing would be beneficial because it'd be responding to something that looks cool on paper or a nebulous desire for more Exalts. The question of their further development should wait until a few years down the line to see if they're still part of the conversation and holding their own once more old favourites have returned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, a lot of things have been the subject of a lot of conversation that still don't really belong in the game line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cust